# Stablecoin Regulation
blockchain:StablecoinRegulation rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Stablecoin Regulation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Stablecoin regulation addresses how jurisdictions govern CryptoToken designed to maintain stable value relative to fiat currencies, commodities, or baskets of assets, balancing financial stability concerns against innovation incentives and payment system benefits. Regulatory frameworks range from the EUMiCA creating explicit categories for EMoneyToken and AssetReferencedToken, to US-based fragmented approaches applying SecuritiesLaw, banking, and money transmission regulations concurrently. Critical compliance requirements including full reserve backing, independent attestations, redemption rights, and AMLKYCCompliance screening aim to address systemic risks demonstrated by the TerraUSD whilst enabling compliant stablecoins like Circle and Tether to function as critical cryptocurrency infrastructure."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stablecoin Regulation"@en ;
    vcw:canonicalUri "urn:visionclaw:concept:blockchain:stablecoin-regulation" ;
    owl:sameAs <urn:visionclaw:concept:blockchain:stablecoin-regulation> ;
    vcw:contentHash "sha256-12-af8ea233e3c4" ;
